WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.310
SAEGUSA SEMINAR

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.940
SELF-STUDY ROOM

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.830
<i>Th-This is awkward.</i>

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.420
STANDING ROOM ONLY
SOBA AJU

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:59.050
EPISODE 12:
SOMETIMES A GENIUS
TRAVELS DOWN
MEMORY LANE WITH X

00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:59.430
It's awkward when they're alone together?

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.140
Right...

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:06.770
Again, I'm talking about my friend
and a girl he's known since middle school.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:10.520
<i>Oh, he must be talking about
himself and Uruka.</i>

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:15.730
He asked her something like,
"Am I the guy you like?"

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.200
But she denied it, so now
he doesn't know how to act around her.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:23.870
What's wrong?

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.700
P-Please, continue.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.710
There's like a weird vibe between them now,
so it probably bothers her, too.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.710
It's fine when they're in a group, though.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:37.050
<i>A major event like that happened
and I didn't even know it.</i>

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:44.470
<i>I wonder why Uruka denied it.</i>

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.020
UME-EN

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:50.060
So she denied it!

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.730
She didn't want it to be a burden for him.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:58.530
I mean, to be honest, I...
I mean, it was my friend's fault for wimping out!

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:02.410
Remember, we're talking about
my friend here, okay?

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.120
R-Right.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:10.250
<i>Jeez, I'm really supposed to be on a diet.</i>

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:11.420
But...

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:17.090
maybe Nari...
I mean, that boy might be frustrated with her.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:21.840
Maybe he hates m... his friend now.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.260
I keep thinking about it.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.140
They can't talk to each other normally,
like they used to.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:32.650
<i>If I'm too supportive of Uruka,
it's not fair to Ri, but...</i>

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.940
<i>It's no good if it has an effect on her studies,</i>

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.280
<i>so maybe I'll pitch in and help just this once.</i>

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:42.820
Say, Uruka...

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:47.160
I think avoiding someone
because you're afraid it could get awkward

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.580
only makes the situation
even more awkward.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:56.130
So why don't the two of you meet
somewhere and have a conversation?

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.720
If you throw yourself into it,

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:05.220
you'll be back to having normal
conversations before you know it.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:12.100
I mean, tell that to your friend.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:16.400
IKEYU PARK

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:16.400
THE NEXT DAY

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.480
Okay, okay.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:29.080
S-So you're busy with your club.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:31.160
That must be tough,
even though it's summer vacation.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:35.120
Y-Yeah. It's because
we have a tournament coming up.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.710
<i>S-So awkward.</i>

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.720
<i>I tried to throw myself into it like
Fuminocchi said and invited him,</i>

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.680
<i>but it's not working at all!</i>

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.560
<i>Come to think of it, before, Furuhashi said...</i>

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.680
<i>If there's any trouble,
just send a text to my phone anytime.</i>

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:56.020
<i>That's what she said, right?</i>

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:57.150
<i>Furuhashi!</i>

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:58.940
<i>Fuminocchi!</i>

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:06.740
<i>Help! My friend is alone with that girl,
but can't think of what to say!</i>

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:08.870
<i>Fuminocchi!
Help!</i>

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:12.750
<i>My friend says she's with that boy now,
but doesn't know what to do!</i>

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:16.540
<i>I came here because
I was worried about them...</i>

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:20.590
<i>but maybe I'm a little too close.</i>

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:21.670
<i>Well...</i>

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:22.380
<i>Luxuriant!</i>

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:23.460
BANGS IN FRONT

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:24.590
<i>Gleam!</i>

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:25.470
FAKE GLASSES

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:26.800
<i>Boom!</i>

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.550
STUFFED WITH SIX BRA PADS

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:32.220
<i>It should be okay since I'm in a good disguise.</i>

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.310
<i>Why not talk about someone you both know?</i>

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:41.650
<i>That could prime the conversational pump.</i>

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:44.030
<i>Someone we both know...</i>

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:47.200
Asumi's family!

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:49.740
I was surprised
her dad's a doctor, you know?

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:50.990
Y-Yeah!

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:55.000
Boy, remember the downpour
we got caught in that day?

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.040
<i>There you go, Yuiga!</i>

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.670
That reminds me...

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.840
Our shirts were all see-through...

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:05.880
You saw, didn't you?

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:12.300
I thought I heard
Furuhashi's voice just now.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.930
Now that you mention it...

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:15.060
<i>Sh-Shoot!</i>

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.060
<i>Is my cover blown?</i>

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:22.230
Oh! It's definitely not her!

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:23.980
Right. Of course it's not.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:28.740
<i>I'm glad they didn't realize it was me,
but I'll give them a pinch later.</i>

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:33.700
<i>They've stopped talking again!</i>

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:40.580
<i>Furuhashi! We were on a roll there,
but then the mood got awkward again!</i>

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:41.790
<i>I mean, for my friend!</i>

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.170
<i>Fuminocchi!</i>

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:46.630
<i>A weird comment slipped out
and the conversation ground to a halt!</i>

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:47.420
My friend's comment!

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:51.930
<i>This "my friend" ruse
is getting weaker by the minute.</i>

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:54.640
<i>All right, you two!</i>

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:57.600
<i>Since it's come to this,
I'm going to get serious!</i>

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:00.980
<i>You should talk about something
that relates to studying.</i>

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:04.020
<i>Like how about something
you often use while at your desk?</i>

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:09.320
Oh yeah, that pen case you gave me
is really convenient. Thanks.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:11.950
Really?! I'm glad to hear it!

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:14.580
After realizing I accidentally
handed you the wrong bag...

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:20.870
I didn't know what to do...

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.330
<i>Huh?</i>

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:27.460
<i>Word has it there's a shrine in the neighborhood
that's effective for improving academic results.</i>

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:29.630
<i>Why don't you two check it out?</i>

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:37.770
The outfit you were wearing
at the shrine last time...

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:40.480
Did the guy you like
get a chance to see it?

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:42.190
Yeah.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:43.850
Oh.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:47.690
END OF CONVERSATION

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.690
<i>Why?</i>

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:52.200
<i>Why does every single topic
backfire with them?</i>

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:55.660
<i>The mood is getting darker and darker!</i>

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:59.250
<i>Furu... Help...</i>

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:03.580
<i>I... don't know... conversation...</i>

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:08.460
<i>They've both blown a fuse.
They can't even form sentences now.</i>

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:14.260
<i>Say, Uruka...</i>

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:20.100
<i>I wonder how your friend
wants that boy to feel about her.</i>

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:22.230
<i>Does she want him to like her?</i>

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:28.480
<i>Yes, she wants that.
Of course.</i>

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:31.150
<i>She's liked him since middle school.</i>

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:35.240
<i>She likes him so much
that she doesn't even know why anymore.</i>

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:37.200
<i>But it wouldn't work.</i>

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:40.790
<i>He's somebody who's always
burning the candle at both ends.</i>

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:45.790
<i>If it would be a burden on him,
it's better that he thinks she likes someone else,</i>

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:48.750
<i>at least until entrance exams are over.</i>

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:53.300
<i>So if... if it's possible...</i>

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.300
<i>I'd like us to go back
to our previous relationship</i>

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:04.060
<i>and it would be nice if every once
in a while, he thought I was cute.</i>

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:09.270
<i>I guess that would be
the happiest outcome for me right now.</i>

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:13.190
<i>I mean, that's what
my friend told me! My friend!</i>

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:16.360
<i>Oh, Uruka...</i>

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:20.160
<i>It's adorable how innocent you are!</i>

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.580
<i>You even make me feel bashful!</i>

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:24.290
<i>But Uruka...</i>

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:29.590
<i>Tell your friend she should really clear up
the mistaken idea that she likes another boy.</i>

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:32.170
<i>I think she can go back
to being friends with him,</i>

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:34.800
<i>even after sharing her true feelings.</i>

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.300
AN IMAGE HAS BEEN SENT TO YOU

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:39.260
<i>What is it,
at an important time like this?</i>

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:41.010
<i>From Sawako?</i>

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:45.060
<i>Hey, which hairstyle do you think
Rizu Ogata would prefer?</i>

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:46.480
<i>Pineapple!</i>

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:47.440
<i>Ponytail!</i>

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:51.110
<i>Or maybe my usual bun style is sexy?</i>

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:53.150
<i>It interminably doesn't matter.</i>

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:54.820
<i>Um, okay...</i>

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:59.410
<i>You should ask Yuiga
how he really feels about you...</i>

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:02.080
<i>Sawako's hairstyle...</i>

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.200
<i>Uruka's misunderstanding...</i>

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.250
TO SAWAKO

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:14.210
<i>I sent them to the wrong person!</i>

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:16.340
<i>Wh-What should I do?!</i>

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.550
<i>Cancel! Cancel!</i>

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:19.640
Takemoto.

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:25.770
That hairstyle suits you.
I mean, it's cute.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.520
Say that again.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:35.320
Oh, that was just...

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:38.450
I mean, I'm sure hearing it from me
doesn't make you happy, right?

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:39.450
Oh, shut up!

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:40.950
Just do it!

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:44.990
I-It looks cute.

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:49.120
One more time.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:51.210
It's cute.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:53.170
One more time!

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:54.420
I said, you look cute.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.300
Once more!

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:58.920
H-Haven't I said it enough?
Now I'm embarrassed!

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.640
Oh, come on! Once more!

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:03.640
I don't want to!

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:05.100
<i>Huh?</i>

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:05.970
Hurry up!

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:09.600
<i>I feel like we're talking normally
to each other again.</i>

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:13.520
<i>Thanks to Master Furuhashi! But...</i>

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:16.610
<i>why a ponytail?</i>

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:23.490
<i>I-It worked out in the end.</i>

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:25.160
<i>I was a nervous wreck.</i>

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:27.490
SAEGUSA SEMINAR

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.490
THE NEXT DAY

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:29.370
Furuhashi!

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.870
You were a big help yesterday!

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:34.630
Thanks to you,
we can to talk to each other naturally again.

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:37.210
I mean, my friend told me
to tell you that.

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:38.670
Glad to hear it.

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:45.390
Wh-What's wrong?

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:56.690
I don't have much money,
but can I pay you back at a stand-up soba place?

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.990
I'm not asking to be compensated!

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:05.320
Anyway, I don't care what happens in the end.

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:06.830
I don't.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:15.040
<i>Could you please formally become my friend?</i>

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:28.510
<i>Take your mark.</i>

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:35.730
Takemoto! Takemoto!

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:40.230
Takemoto! Takemoto! Takemoto!

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:43.030
She did it!

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:47.990
Takemoto of Ichinose Academy
won the 200-meter freestyle!

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:51.660
Ichinose Academy's doing really well.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.910
Maybe they'll win the relay, too.

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:05.180
Ikedacchi, it's almost time.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:06.550
R-Right!

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:22.480
AKAHORI NATATORIUM

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:22.480
Ichinose Academy was so close.

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:24.900
Too bad they were disqualified
for that false start.

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:29.030
Yeah, that second-year dove in before
the previous swimmer touched the wall.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.250
Come on, stop crying, Ikeda.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:39.340
Yeah, it can't be helped.

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:43.800
I'm sorry! This was your last tournament
before your graduation!

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:46.470
But because of me...

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:48.050
Hey, Ikedacchi.

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:51.720
I'm not going to tell you
that it's no big deal.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:54.730
You should cry your eyes out
and feel frustrated as hell.

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:57.100
R-Right.

00:13:57.230 --> 00:14:01.480
But after that, I'm sure
you won't screw up next time, right?

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:04.820
The swim club needs you.

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:08.740
Senpai!

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:20.290
Jeez, I said you didn't have to come,
not when you had prep school.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:23.800
I know.
I just felt like I had to go.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:27.970
<i>"So close."
"You really did your best."</i>

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:31.890
<i>No, that all sounds lame.</i>

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:36.600
Hey, what's got you
on the brink of tears, Nariyuki?

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:39.270
I-I'm not on the brink of tears!

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:43.940
I mean, sorry.
You're probably the one who wants to cry.

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:50.030
True.
I wanted us to all win together.

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:56.040
But if Ikedacchi learns
from what happened today,

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.460
then it won't have been in vain.

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:05.340
Besides, there are some people
who want to cry a lot more than I do.

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:08.090
So for me...

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:16.390
If I'm going to cry, I'll do everything I can first,
and then cry my heart out.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:19.060
And when I do, lend me your shoulder, okay?

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.350
Just kidding!

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:25.860
Still, thank you, Nariyuki.

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:27.690
You were trying to encourage me, right?

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:30.240
Well, yeah, that was the idea...

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:35.990
If you still want to try and cheer me up...

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:39.540
would you hang out with me tonight?

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:47.050
This is our old middle school.

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:52.340
This brings back memories!

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:55.100
Not much has changed
in three years, huh?

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.560
So what are we doing here?

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.060
Hey, do you remember this?

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.690
Our desks were next to each other, right?

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:05.650
Yeah, for the first term of our first year.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:08.230
I remember the first time I saw you.

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:12.740
Who would've thought that gloomy,
four-eyed bookworm would be so...

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:14.320
Be so what?

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:19.580
I never thought you'd be so easy to talk to!

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:23.750
Hey, where are we going now?

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.460
A good place.

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:45.350
<i>Ever since that day, I always
found myself on the lookout for him.</i>

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:48.860
<i>N-Nariyuki!</i>

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:50.860
<i>No, that's not right.</i>

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:53.360
<i>Wh-What's up, Nariyuki?</i>

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:58.870
<i>I practiced in front of a mirror
at home so I could greet him naturally.</i>

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:04.870
This feels great!

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:10.710
Man, I'm glad they didn't change
the pool key's hiding place.

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:13.340
Okay, so why are we here?

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:16.760
I kind of wanted
to go back to where it all began.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:18.800
I wanted to come here.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:21.970
To this place, with you.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:24.560
With me? Why?

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:27.520
At the beginning
of first year in middle school,

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:32.280
I was thinking of giving up swimming,
but I continued because of you.

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:44.790
Takemoto, why aren't you going
to join the swim club?

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:46.920
When you swim so fast...

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:53.090
In the last tournament of elementary school,
I lost big-time.

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:59.220
After that, I though maybe it's better to swim
for fun, so I won't feel frustrated like that.

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:02.680
<i>What? After just one loss?
That's pathetic!</i>

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:05.230
<i>What's the point if you don't stick to anything?</i>

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:09.020
If losing only once
makes you feel that frustrated,

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:11.820
I bet you must have
a really precious gift.

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:15.490
I'm envious because
I don't have anything like that.

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:21.990
You're so lucky to have something
you can get that serious about.

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:32.090
I think this is the first time
anyone's said something like that.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:33.130
Really?

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:36.760
<i>Something I can get serious about...</i>

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:42.850
You don't remember that?

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:44.970
Sure, we were just chatting.

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:51.810
But you're part of the reason
I can swim like I do, Nariyuki,

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:54.980
so I wanted to say this to you
for the longest time.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:57.190
Thanks.

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:03.830
<i>The guy you like...</i>

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:06.040
<i>Is it me?</i>

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:11.130
<i>Yeah, right!
What are you talking about?</i>

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:15.550
B-By the way, Takemoto...

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:18.300
Have you told him how you feel?

00:19:19.430 --> 00:19:22.850
That guy you like...

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:27.850
I can't! There has been
so many times when I wanted to...

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:32.560
but a lot's been going on
and now is especially a bad time...

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:34.820
S-Sounds like you've got it rough.

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:40.150
<i>I wasn't able to cheer her up
about the swim meet.</i>

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:43.370
<i>Isn't there anything
I can do for Takemoto?</i>

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:47.870
All right! Takemoto!

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:50.460
Confess your feelings to me!

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:51.790
What are you saying?

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:54.840
I'll be your training partner!
Do a confessional dry run with me

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:57.000
so you don't screw up
during the real thing!

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:59.260
<i>Like I could do that,
Nariyuki, you idiot!</i>

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:01.470
Repetition is the key to everything, Takemoto!

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:05.430
<i>This is the worst time ever
for him to be altruistic!</i>

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:09.930
<i>But that earnest face
of his is so cool!</i>

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:12.350
<i>Since it's come to this...</i>

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:16.480
I-I think mood is really
important for that kind of thing.

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:19.820
Maybe if you called me by my first name...

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:22.860
<i>If you ask the impossible of me,
I'll ask the impossible of you!</i>

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:24.950
U-Uruka?

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:31.660
<i>Idiot.</i>

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:34.210
<i>Stupid Nariyuki.</i>

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:38.340
<i>How?
How could you say it so easily?</i>

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:41.760
<i>You have no idea how much I practiced</i>

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:44.800
<i>before I was able to say "Nariyuki."</i>

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:51.890
<i>I just got done saying I wasn't going to cry,
but I'm so frustrated that I'm tearing up.</i>

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:55.810
<i>Ugh, my mind's gone blank.</i>

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:59.070
Nariyuki...

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:06.910
I like you.
In fact, I really like you, Nariyuki.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:14.290
<i>Huh? I didn't...
Did I just... Crap.</i>

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:16.130
<i>I seriously confess—</i>

00:21:16.130 --> 00:21:17.330
Takemoto.

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:22.210
Why don't you try that once more?

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:27.720
I mean, your confession was great,
but you're not supposed to say my name!

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:30.890
Other than that, you totally nailed it!

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:41.570
What was that for, Takemoto?

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:43.240
Takemoto?

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:50.620
Huh? I thought you were going
to start calling me by my first name.

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:54.210
Okay then. Uruka.

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:01.210
Takemoto!

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:39.560
Next time: The Light in a Genius's Eye Is All X.

00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:40.060
NEXT EPISODE: THE LIGHT
IN A GENIUS'S EYE IS ALL X
